+
+    FP8 has a primary per-tensor tile with kN0 > 64 so both buffer-load and
+    large-cache global-load variants are emitted.  The final FP8 tile preserves
+    the already-qualified padded-V192 route.  BF16 uses native V128 and falls
+    back to the D256 page-64 family for padded V192.
+    """
+    if target is None:
+        return []
+    if dtype == "bf16":
